; Manifest-phase family, 1 of 6 — and one of the two that are *advisory*.
;
; `:license` is not checked against any registry beyond the canonical SPDX
; identifier list, and a miss is a warning: the manifest still loads, the
; plugin still joins the schema, and `(pt :x 1)` below still validates. That
; is the whole point of pairing this case with the four error-severity ones
; in the same batch — severity here is not a label on the message, it
; decides whether the plugin survives. The error cases each carry a trailing
; `unknown_form` for exactly that reason; this one does not.
(plugin :name probe :version "1.0.0" :license "Squiggle-2.0"
  (form :name pt (key :name x :type number)))

(pt :x 1)
